# Important DAX Functions
## SUM

The `SUM` function in DAX is used to add all numeric values from a column in a table. 
It is one of the most basic and widely used aggregation functions in Power BI. 
SUM works only with numerical data types such as integers, decimals, or currency values.
Blank values are ignored automatically during the calculation process. This function is
commonly used in business reports to calculate total sales, total profit, total quantity, and other financial values. 
SUM helps users quickly analyze overall performance in dashboards and visualizations. It can also be combined with other
DAX functions like CALCULATE and FILTER to perform advanced calculations. The function improves data summarization and 
simplifies reporting tasks. Because of its simplicity and efficiency, SUM is frequently used in measures and calculated 
columns. In Power BI, SUM plays an important role in creating KPIs and business metrics. It is highly useful in finance, sales, inventory,
and accounting analysis where total values are required for decision-making and reporting purposes.

```DAX id="a2s9yw"
Total Sales = SUM(Sales[Amount])
```

