## AVERAGE

The `AVERAGE` function in DAX is used to calculate the arithmetic mean of numeric values in a column. It adds all values and divides
them by the number of non-blank entries. This function works only with numeric data types and automatically ignores blank values during 
calculation. AVERAGE is commonly used in reports where performance analysis is required, such as average salary, average marks, average sales,
or average customer ratings. It helps organizations understand trends and patterns in data. The function is simple to use and provides meaningful 
insights into business performance. AVERAGE is widely used in statistical analysis and dashboard reporting because it gives a clear understanding 
of central values in a dataset. It can also be combined with filters and conditions to calculate averages for specific categories or time periods.
In Power BI, AVERAGE helps users make better business decisions by identifying typical performance values. It is especially useful in education, 
finance, healthcare, and sales analysis where average-based comparisons are important.

```DAX id="eqdzv5"
Average Salary = AVERAGE(Employee[Salary])
```

