## COUNT

The `COUNT` function in DAX is used to count the number of rows containing numeric values in a specific column. It ignores blank
and non-numeric values automatically. COUNT is useful for analyzing records and understanding how many entries are available in a dataset. 
This function is commonly used in attendance systems, product analysis, sales reports, and customer databases. It helps businesses measure 
data volume and identify the number of valid records. COUNT works on a single column and is easy to implement in measures and calculated columns. 
The function is important in data summarization because it provides quick numerical analysis for reports and dashboards. In Power BI, 
COUNT helps users monitor transactions, orders, employees, and other business activities. It can also be combined with filters and logical 
conditions to count records based on specific criteria. COUNT improves reporting accuracy and supports better data-driven decision-making processes 
in organizations by providing meaningful statistical information about datasets.

```DAX id="jvqyn4"
Product Count = COUNT(Product[ProductID])
```

