## IF

The `IF` function in DAX is used to test a condition and return different values depending on whether the condition is true or false.
It is one of the most important logical functions in Power BI and is commonly used for decision-making calculations. IF works similarly 
to conditional statements in programming languages. Businesses use this function to categorize data, create labels, and perform conditional 
analysis. For example, sales values can be classified as high or low depending on a target amount. The function improves report interactivity
and helps create meaningful calculated columns and measures. IF can also be nested inside another IF function to handle multiple conditions, 
although SWITCH is usually preferred for many conditions. In Power BI dashboards, IF helps users identify performance levels, employee status,
grades, and customer categories. The function is easy to understand and widely used in finance, education, sales, and HR analysis.
IF provides flexibility and improves the overall analytical capabilities of DAX formulas.

```DAX id="7f7mls"
Status = IF(Sales[Amount] > 5000, "High", "Low")
```

