## SWITCH

The `SWITCH` function in DAX is used to evaluate multiple conditions and return corresponding results. It is considered a better alternative 
to multiple nested IF statements because it makes formulas simpler, cleaner, and easier to read. SWITCH compares an expression against several 
values and returns the matching result. This function is commonly used in grading systems, performance analysis, category mapping, and status
reporting. In Power BI, SWITCH helps reduce formula complexity and improves maintainability of reports. It is especially useful when there are
many conditions to evaluate. The function enhances readability and makes debugging easier for developers and analysts. SWITCH can also include a
default value if no condition matches the expression. Businesses use this function to classify customers, products, employees, and sales performance 
into different groups. It supports efficient business analysis and improves report organization. SWITCH is widely used in dashboards because it
simplifies logic creation and enhances overall reporting quality in Power BI solutions.

```DAX id="9y6z5m"
Grade =
SWITCH(
    Student[Marks],
    90, "A",
    80, "B",
    70, "C"
)
```
